<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CRA signs A$800 mln iron ore contract.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CRA signs A$800 mln iron ore contract.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>CRA Ltd-RTZ Corp Plc said on Monday it had signed a A$800 million contract with China Steel of Taiwan to supply iron ore to the Taiwanese steelmaker.  </p>
<p>CRA-RTZ unit Hamersley Iron Pty Ltd said the renewed contract covering the next 10 years would result in Hamersley supplying over 32 million tonnes of iron ore to China Steel in Kaohsiung between April 1997 and March 2007, RTZ-CRA said.</p>
<p>These new export sales will be worth over A$800 million, it said. As a result of the agreement, Hamersley will double the level of shipments to 70 million tonnes during the next 10 years, RTZ-CRA said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
